  "id": "Compound::DB00203 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Sildenafil is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2d6 through multiple indirect pathways, primarily involving the binding of heterocyclic compounds. The evidence suggests that Sildenafil may act as a modulator of Cyp2d6 through its interaction with organonitrogen heterocyclic compounds, which are common in the pharmacological profile of Sildenafil. This is supported by the observed binding of Hydroxychloroquine and Chloroquine to Cyp2d6, both of which are organonitrogen heterocyclic compounds, and the indirect causation of these compounds by Sildenafil. Additionally, the presence of Rifapentine, another organonitrogen heterocyclic compound, further reinforces the role of Sildenafil in the regulation of Cyp2d6 through a chain of interactions involving these compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Sildenafil influences Cyp2d6, likely through the modulation of heterocyclic compound binding and subsequent enzymatic activity.",
